description: Testing rules for AutoWave (PHPUnit on PostgreSQL)
globs: tests/**/*.php,phpunit.xml
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- Tests run on PostgreSQL database `autowave_testing` (see `phpunit.xml`). Never switch to SQLite.
- Run `php artisan test` before every commit. CI runs Pint + tests + frontend build.
- Use `RefreshDatabase` for tests that touch the database. Use factories, not hand-written inserts.
- `tests/TestCase.php` disables Vite so backend tests never need `npm run build`.
- Organise by domain: `tests/Feature/<Domain>/...`, `tests/Unit/<Domain>/...`.
- Every tenant-owned feature needs isolation tests:

```php
public function test_tenant_a_cannot_view_tenant_b_lead(): void
{
    [$tenantA, $userA] = $this->tenantWithOwner();
    $leadB = Lead::factory()->for(Tenant::factory())->create();

    $this->actingAs($userA)->onTenant($tenantA)
        ->get(route('leads.show', $leadB))
        ->assertNotFound();
}
```

- Every permission-guarded action needs allowed + forbidden tests.
- Booking: create, cancel, reschedule, unavailable slot, duplicate, concurrent attempt, timezone.
- Automation: trigger, condition pass/fail, delay, execution, retry, failure log, duplicate prevention.
- Fake external providers (`Http::fake()`, `Queue::fake()`, `Notification::fake()`); never call real APIs.
- Never delete or weaken a test to make the suite pass.
